From: box86-16k contributors
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] BRIDGE: size bridge bricks to the host page

Box86 allocates bridge thunks in hard-coded 4K bricks.  That matches the
traditional host page size, but on a 16K host each 4K mmap/munmap request is
backed by an entire 16K kernel page while Box86 only accounts for 4K of it.

Box64 already sizes NBRICK from box64_pagesize.  Do the equivalent in Box86 so
a bridge brick always occupies exactly one host page.  On 4K hosts this is a
no-op; on 16K hosts it keeps bridge allocation, protection tracking and
unmapping on the same granularity as the kernel.
---
 src/tools/bridge.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/tools/bridge.c b/src/tools/bridge.c
--- a/src/tools/bridge.c
+++ b/src/tools/bridge.c
@@ -21,7 +21,7 @@
 
 KHASH_MAP_INIT_INT(bridgemap, uintptr_t)
 
-#define NBRICK  (4096/sizeof(onebridge_t))
+#define NBRICK  (box86_pagesize/sizeof(onebridge_t))
 typedef struct brick_s brick_t;
 typedef struct brick_s {
     onebridge_t *b;
